'''Wood''' or '''hyphae''' is a [[block]] that has the [[log]]'s "bark" texture on all six sides. It comes in 12 types: [[oak]], [[spruce]], [[birch]], [[jungle tree|jungle]], [[acacia]], [[dark oak]], [[mangrove]], [[cherry]], [[huge crimson fungus|crimson]], [[huge warped fungus|warped]], [[pale oak]], and [[poplar]].

== Obtaining ==
=== Breaking ===
Wood and hyphae can be broken by hand, but using an [[axe]] is the fastest.
{{breaking row|horizontal=1|Wood, Hyphae|link=none|Axe}}

=== Crafting ===
Wood or hyphae can be crafted out of four matching logs or stems, yielding three wood or hyphae as a result.
{{Crafting
|A1=Matching Log; Matching Stem
|A2=Matching Log; Matching Stem
|B1=Matching Log; Matching Stem
|B2=Matching Log; Matching Stem
|Output=Matching Wood,3; Matching Hyphae,3
|type=Building block
}}

=== Natural generation ===
Acacia wood can generate in [[savanna]] [[village]]s.

Spruce wood can generate in [[snowy taiga]] and [[taiga]] villages.

Mangrove wood can generate in some entrance rooms of [[trial chambers]].

== Usage ==
Wood and hyphae can be placed in three orientations, similarly to normal [[log]]s.

=== Crafting ingredient ===
{{crafting usage|Any Wood, Any Hyphae, Any Wood or Hyphae, Matching Wood, Matching Hyphae}}

=== Smelting ingredient ===
{{Smelting
|showname=1
|{Any Wood}
|Charcoal
|0.15
}}

=== Fuel ===
Wood can be used as a [[fuel]] in [[furnace]]s, smelting 1.5 items per block.

Hyphae cannot be used as a fuel in furnaces.

=== Axes ===
{{Control|Using}} an [[axe]] on wood or hyphae turns it into [[stripped wood]] or hyphae, which acts the same as regular wood or hyphae.

=== Cocoa beans ===
[[Cocoa beans]] can be placed on the side of jungle wood to grow new cocoa pods.

